BT /F4 19 Tf 1 0 0 1 123.4 474.0 Tm (Two Difficult Choices) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 58.0 439.0 Tm (On Thursday, Alice woke before the sun came up. The music was) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 43.0 421.9 Tm (still on the piano. Her shop was full of pictures she had not finished.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 43.0 404.8 Tm (On the table lay the letter about the job in Lyon.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 58.0 377.7 Tm (She opened the letter again. The office wanted an answer by) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 43.0 360.6 Tm (Saturday. The job was good and safe. Alice could pay her bills) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 43.0 343.5 Tm (without worry. But she had to move away from Paris.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 58.0 316.4 Tm (At nine, her mother came to the shop. Anna was sixty-four years) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 43.0 299.3 Tm (old. She had worked in a hospital for many years. Now she liked to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 43.0 282.2 Tm (walk in the park and read in the afternoon.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 58.0 255.1 Tm (Alice showed her the letter. Then she told her about the theatre.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 43.0 238.0 Tm (Anna listened without speaking. She put her hand over Alice's hand.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 43.0 220.9 Tm ('You have two important things to think about,' she said.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 58.0 193.8 Tm ('One is a good job,' Alice said. 'The other is only a little show.') Tj ET
BT /F1 11.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 43.0 176.7 Tm (Anna shook her head. 'Do not call a thing little because it does not) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 43.0 159.6 Tm (bring much money. But do not forget your work either.') Tj ET
BT /F1 11.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 58.0 132.5 Tm (They sat by the window and watched people go to the market.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 43.0 115.4 Tm (Alice remembered the music lessons her father had paid for when) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 43.0 98.3 Tm (money was short. He had said that work and beauty could live in the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 43.0 81.2 Tm (same home.) Tj ET
